## 6. Service Orchestration & Systemd Security Hardening

<comment-tag id="4" text="Document troubleshooting steps using journalctl -u wg-mullvad.service -e to quickly inspect service failure reasons during sandbox rejections or permission issues." type="suggestion">Both wg-mullvad.service and wg-recovery.service employ strict capability bounds and sandboxing primitives.</comment-tag id="4">

### Main VPN Service (`systemd/wg-mullvad.service`)

```
[Unit]
Description=WireGuard VPN (Mullvad) tunnel
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=exec
ExecStart=/usr/bin/wg-quick up wg0
ExecStop=/usr/bin/wg-quick down wg0
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5

CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_NET_ADMIN CAP_NET_RAW
AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_ADMIN CAP_NET_RAW

ProtectSystem=full
PrivateTmp=yes
ProtectHome=yes
ReadWritePaths=/etc/wireguard
NoNewPrivileges=yes

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target


```

## 7. Automated Health Checks & Interface Verification

To prevent silent failures (a "dead tunnel" where the interface is up but routing fails), the test suite utilizes interface-bound inspection.

### Interface-Based DNS Leak Test (`scripts/dns-leak-test.sh`)

```
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

source "$(dirname "$0")/wg-env.sh"

require_cmd() { command -v "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "Missing command: $1"; exit 1; }; }
require_cmd dig
require_cmd tcpdump
require_cmd ip
require_cmd grep

WG_IFACE="${WG_IFACE:-wg0}"
DNS_SERVER="${WG_DNS}"

ip link show "$WG_IFACE" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "Interface $WG_IFACE not found"; exit 1; }
[[ -n "${DNS_SERVER}" ]] || { echo "WG_DNS is empty"; exit 1; }

TMP="$(mktemp)"
trap 'rm -f "$TMP"' EXIT

sudo tcpdump -i "$WG_IFACE" -n -l "host ${DNS_SERVER} and port 53" >"$TMP" 2>/dev/null &
TCPDUMP_PID=$!

sleep 1
dig @"$DNS_SERVER" example.com +time=2 +tries=1 +short >/dev/null 2>&1 || true

sudo kill "$TCPDUMP_PID" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
wait "$TCPDUMP_PID" 2>/dev/null || true

if grep -q "$DNS_SERVER" "$TMP"; then
  echo "PASS: DNS traffic to ${DNS_SERVER} observed on ${WG_IFACE}"
  exit 0
else
  echo "FAIL: No DNS traffic to ${DNS_SERVER} observed on ${WG_IFACE}"
  exit 1
fi


```

### Handshake Freshness Test (`scripts/handshake-freshness-test.sh`)

```
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

source "$(dirname "$0")/wg-env.sh"

require_cmd() { command -v "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo "Missing command: $1"; exit 1; }; }
require_cmd wg
require_cmd awk
require_cmd date

WG_IFACE="${WG_IFACE:-wg0}"
MAX_AGE_SEC="${MAX_HANDSHAKE_AGE_SEC:-120}"

LATEST_TS="$(sudo wg show "$WG_IFACE" 2>/dev/null | awk '/latest handshake:/ {print $3}' | head -n1)"

if [[ -z "$LATEST_TS" || "$LATEST_TS" == "0" ]]; then
  echo "FAIL: No active handshake detected on ${WG_IFACE}"
  exit 1
fi

NOW_TS="$(date +%s)"
AGE_SEC="$((NOW_TS - LATEST_TS))"

if [[ "$AGE_SEC" -le "$MAX_AGE_SEC" ]]; then
  echo "PASS: Latest handshake age is ${AGE_SEC}s (<= ${MAX_AGE_SEC}s)"
  exit 0
else
  echo "FAIL: Handshake stale. Age: ${AGE_SEC}s (> ${MAX_AGE_SEC}s)"
  exit 1
fi


```

